    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, when you say \"the benefits were disproportionally reaped by higher income groups,\" doesn't that almost imply the growth itself wasn't \"real\" success? like, if the engine of growth only helps the top 1%, can we really call the policy a win for the economy as a whole, or is it more accurate to say that the policy was fundamentally flawed?",
